  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Music of the Pontic Greeks of the Black Sea coast, transplanted to northern Greece and the diaspora after the 1923 population exchange and sustained at diaspora associations and panigyria — the three-string bowed kemenche (Pontian lyra) playing continuous fast double-stopped melody with a droning lower string, driving the tik, omal and serra dances in 5/8 and 7/8 at high tempo, doubled at open-air events by zurna and davul, with strophic distich singing",
